# A standard stream over a terminal hands native code the function that reads the size anew, by a call of a native function of the library's own. No code in sight calls the function: it has left to code that nobody sees, so it is reached and not every caller of it is known.
# The call names neither `process` nor `on`: of the native emitter nothing is in use, and what stands for it is the feature that the row of the native function names.
#   listenForSizeOfTerminal(() => { refreshed = true; });
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK-NOT: function f2 unreached
# CHECK-NOT: function f2 callers-known
# RUN(FEATURES): features
# REQUIRES(FEATURES): entries-of-bun
# FEATURES: by NativeNewCppFunctionBunProcessCppJsFunctionListenForSizeOfTerminal
# FEATURES-NOT: by EventEmitterPrototype

variable g0 name="refreshed" module=m1 declared={type=anything}
module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
module m1 path="node:http" displayPath="node:http" kind=RuntimeSource exportRule=RuntimeModule requireResult=DefaultExport runtimeModule=NodeHttp body=f1
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = RequireModule module=m1 referrer=m0 specifier="node:http"
    v1 = Undefined
    Return v1
}
function f1 module=m1 kind=Module role=Library thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = NativeBinding builtin=NativeNewCppFunctionBunProcessCppJsFunctionListenForSizeOfTerminal
    v1 = NewClosure function=f2
    v2 = Call v0, -, v1 calleeName="listenForSizeOfTerminal"
    v3 = Undefined
    Return v3
}
function f2 module=m1 kind=Arrow role=Library thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Boolean boolean=true
    PutModuleVariable v0 variable=g0
    v2 = Undefined
    Return v2
}
